        derives_from [
                     @plan.PackageContract.O1,
                     @plan.PackageContract.O2,
                     @plan.PackageContract.V1,
                     @plan.PackageContract.D1,
                     @plan.PackageContract.D2,
                     @plan.PackageContract.C2,
                     @plan.PackageContract.C3,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O1,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V1
                     ]
        description
            Deliverable: root, react, testing, and inspect routes expose settled named exports;
            Q2-bound Inspection names remain omitted until T609; Q2/Q4-bound model names remain
            omitted until T610.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/package.json, src/index.ts,
            src/react-entry.ts, src/testing.ts, src/inspect.ts, quickstart, CLI bin metadata, and
            route/quickstart packed tests. T601 is the sole package.json and route-entrypoint
            writer.
            Evidence: per-route runtime/declaration maps, quickstart compile, and packed consumer
            receipts;
            evidence/T601.md.
            1. Add the four route shells and settled named exports after each semantic owner exists.
            2. Compile quickstart, strict isolated consumers, and React 18/19 packed consumers.
            3. Verify package bin metadata targets the settled CLI command entry.
            4. Reject namespace objects, deep imports, undeclared names, and unresolved forms.
            Prerequisite rationale: T108 is the initial route gate; capability and artifact owners
            provide
            the names/declarations consumed here. Public package checks continue with each API
            change.
            Local deferral: InspectionAndArtifacts Q2 and StoriesAndModels Q2/Q4 leave named forms
            open; T609 and T610 own their later reachability proofs.
            Shared-write boundary: capability Tasks own API declarations; only T601 edits route
            files.
        acceptance
            Exactly four route shells resolve; only settled names are exported and Q2-bound names
            remain deferred to the named reachability proof Tasks T609/T610. Root/non-root route
            boundaries, package namespaces, and deep
            imports match the Plan. React 18/19 and isolated declaration consumers compile against
            settled packed output; quickstart compiles without any/assertion erasure.
            Run rewrite check:types, build, and check:packed-consumers; expected: all pass.

    T602
        title        Portable shared-codec host vectors
        status       open
        priority     medium
        blocked_by   [@task.Rewrite.T107, @task.Rewrite.T409]
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PackageContract.C1,
                     @plan.PackageContract.V2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.O2,
                     @plan.InspectionAndArtifacts.V2
                     ]
        description
            Deliverable: the same compiled shared codec produces equal accepted bytes across
            supported hosts.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/test/portable-codec/**; do not edit codec
            owners.
            Evidence: exact runtime/browser versions, vectors, bytes or digests, and failure
            receipts;
            evidence/T602.md.
            1. Run full ASCII, multibyte, composed/decomposed, 256/257-byte, and lone-surrogate
            vectors
            on pinned Node.
            2. Run compact vectors through the same codec on Bun, Deno, Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit.
            3. Record exact versions and compare accepted bytes; route any defect to T107/T409
            owners.
            Prerequisites: P1 owns codec core and P4 owns its bounded envelope integration.
            Shared-write boundary: add host harnesses only; never add a second handwritten encoder.
        acceptance
            Every host uses the same compiled codec and accepted input produces equal canonical
            bytes.
            Lone surrogates and invalid limits fail before serialization or activation.
            The full vector set passes on pinned Node and compact set passes on each recorded host.
            Run host vector suites; expected: byte equality and pre-mutation rejection.

    T603
        title        Surface disposition map
        status       open
        priority     medium
        derives_from [
                     @plan.PackageContract.O3,
                     @plan.PackageContract.V3,
                     @plan.PackageContract.D1,
                     @plan.PackageContract.C3
                     ]
        description
            Deliverable: a row-by-row map for PackageContract DEL-001 through DEL-011 and RET-001
            through
            RET-005, with one new semantic owner and proof Task per live obligation.
            Allowed writes: workflow/tasks/Rewrite/evidence/surface-disposition.md only.
            Evidence: completed row map and reviewer observations in that file.
            1. Read the new PackageContract Plan disposition rows and current new capability
            Plans/Tasks.
            2. Map each row to DELETE/REPLACE/RETAIN/HISTORICAL and its new owner/proof obligations.
            3. Flag unmapped consumers or duplicated ownership; do not edit source or historical
            records.
            Prerequisite rationale: no implementation proof is required; this map consumes only the
            new PackageContract and capability Plans/Tasks. It can proceed before implementation
            proofs and does not establish absence.
            Shared-write boundary: this Task is read-only apart from its evidence map; it does not
            edit source or historical records.
            No Beads, former contract pack, old Plan status, or historical Task status is evidence.
        acceptance
            Every DEL/RET row has an explicit disposition, one semantic owner, and a named proof
            Task or a
            clear unresolved owner gap.
            No row claims runtime/declaration absence, retained behavior, cutover, or cleanup from
            a map alone.
            Review the complete row map against PackageContract O3; expected: no omitted or
            multiply owned
            obligation.

