        description
            Deliverable: a packed consumer authors a bounded dropping/coalescing feed without Flow
            pressure
            options or a competing stream scheduler.
            Allowed writes: packages/flow-state-rewrite/test/packed/feed/** only.
            Evidence: authored feed, slow-consumer observations, release receipts; evidence/T605.md.
            1. Build the feed solely from accepted stream declarations and application-owned policy.
            2. Drive a slower consumer and observe the accepted drop/coalesce behavior.
            3. Dispose the owner and verify the session releases exactly once.
            Prerequisites: P3 stream sessions and integrated actor/store publication; T312 supplies
            the settled authored forms after Streams Q1. T601 provides the packed consumer surface.
            Local question: Streams Q1; keep draft.
            Shared-write boundary: T605 writes the application feed consumer only; stream/runtime
            changes return to P3 owners.
        acceptance
            The consumer authors dropping/coalescing behavior without a Flow pressure option.
            Slow-consumer observations match application policy; Flow exposes no unaccepted queue
            controls.
            Disposal releases the production stream session exactly once.
            Run the packed feed integration test; expected: bounded output and clean release.

