                     @plan.Transactions.O4,
                     @plan.Transactions.V4
                     ]
        description
            Deliverable: Incident Console proves exact bindings, conflicts, streams, inspection,
            diagnostics,
            installed CLI/artifacts, and browser lifetime over accepted routes.
            Allowed writes: reference/incident-console/implementation/test/capability-buildout/**
            and
            packages/flow-state-rewrite/test/packed/incident-console/**.
            Evidence: browser version, packed revision, journeys, interruption/cleanup results;
            evidence/T606.md.
            1. Install the fresh packed package and drive representative console/browser journeys.
            2. Exercise a transaction conflict, stream lifecycle, trace comparison, and CLI failure
            lane.
            3. Record owner Task IDs for each semantic observation and distinguish app failures
            from Flow.
            Prerequisites: route/host/Story/CLI, operation, diagnostic, and artifact owners.
            Shared-write boundary: application-owned tests only; product source fixes return to
            their owners.
        acceptance
            The packed browser journey uses accepted public routes and preserves request/component 
            ownership. Exercise a real application-owned remote lease: while its independent 
            durable journal acknowledgment is pending or failed, assert no remote request is 
            dispatched; after acknowledgment, cancel an invoked/in-flight remote operation and 
            assert the view reports unknown/reconcileRequired, late completion cannot publish, and 
            no rollback is claimed. Reconcile with the same remote identity; compensation, if 
            exercised, is a distinct explicit operation. Also prove transaction conflict/preview 
            behavior, stream lifecycle, inspection/trace comparison, diagnostics, CLI artifacts, 
            and cleanup against their owner Plans, including interruption and finalization results. 
            No private import, old surface, or fabricated failure is used. Run packed application 
            and browser tests; expected: all owner-linked journeys, journal/no-dispatch and 
            remote-lease cases, failures, and cleanup pass.

